## Feasibility (raid 2026-10-27): WARN
- Moving `rules/authoring-skills.md` under `skills/harness-doctor/references/` breaks `make check-agnostic-skills`. Its line 24 has the bare `` `scripts/check-agnostic.sh` ``, which matches SKILL_PATTERNS (positive control run: VIOLATION, exit 1). Fix: write `$IDH_ROOT/scripts/check-agnostic.sh` in the moved text, and the same for every script path in SKILL.md and references (`gen_skills_catalog.py`, `skill_text_lint.py`, `harness_here.sh`).
- Open ticket 1222 (outside this raid) also edits `rules/authoring-skills.md` (one-line convention). Record in the PR that 1222 retargets to the reference file after this move.
- 1234 emits `{"files","findings":[{file,line,check,text}],"summary"}`. Read `.findings[]`, not a top-level list.
- `skills-catalog.md` is gated by `make check-skills-drift`. Regenerate it in the same commit as the new SKILL.md. Category `session` is valid (`gen_skills_catalog.py:21`). This is the only PR in the raid that touches the catalog.
- Other citers verified: test_skill_descriptions.py:3,63; test_skill_frontmatter.py:160; test_check_agnostic.py:272; check-agnostic.sh:25 (comment); rules/README.md:38.
- `claude plugin eval` headless behaviour is unverified. Keep the hand check, and record "unavailable", never "clean". No keys or network otherwise.

**Runtime diagnostics, Claude Code (verified in docs 2026-10-27, raid).** Sources: code.claude.com/docs/en/troubleshooting.md, cli-reference.md, skills.md, plugin-evals.md.
- `claude doctor` (shell): runs without a user, read-only; install health, unparseable settings, unused skills and their context cost, CLAUDE.md duplication, slow hooks. Text output; JSON unverified. Scope is the user's own setup, not an arbitrary directory.
- `/doctor` (in-session): interactive, proposes fixes; the author runs it.
- `/skill-doctor`: per-skill context cost, 7-day usage, never-invoked skills. Not a linter; usage evidence for the doctor. Bash invocation unconfirmed; the author runs it and pastes.
- `claude plugin validate <path>`: structural schema check, no model spend. First choice.
- `claude plugin eval . --json <file> --no-publish --max-cost-usd N`: runs without a user, `schemaVersion: 1` JSON, exits 0/1/2; spends model usage; needs a plugin manifest or skills-dir plugin (loose SKILL.md folders are not auto-detected). Behaviour evals only, opt-in with an explicit cost cap.
Codex and Pi: still to inventory, with a positive control before recording "none".

**Runtime diagnostics, Codex and Pi (probed locally 2026-10-27, codex-cli 0.164.0, pi 1.4.0).** The doctor treats every runtime alike: run what each ships, cheapest first, and report an unavailable tool as unavailable.
- Codex `codex doctor --json`: runs without a user, `schemaVersion` JSON, `overallStatus` plus 21 checks (config.load, mcp.config, sandbox.*, state.*, installation, …). Health of the install, not of skill text.
- Codex `codex debug prompt-input`: runs without a user, no model spend; JSON of the model-visible input, `AGENTS.md` and skills included. The direct evidence of what Codex actually loads, hence of shadowing and precedence: the doctor's best cross-runtime probe, and a candidate input for 1230.
- Codex `codex review`: non-interactive reviewer, model spend; a decorrelated seat, not a diagnostic.
- Pi: no doctor or validate command (the help lists all commands: install, remove, update, list, config, auth, mcp). Available: `pi list` (installed extensions), `pi auth` (provider readiness), `pi mcp` (servers); `pi --skill <path> -p --mode json` loads one skill headless at model cost. Record "no diagnostic" for skill text in Pi, against this command list as the control; web docs not yet checked.
